# Prove the My Abilities help section for ANY loaded character, not just the
# orc barbarian fixture. Fixture-agnostic sibling of char-abilities.keys.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/<name>.sav \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/char-abilities-any.keys 1
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS ALONGSIDE char-abilities.keys. That script proves the My
# Character page's My Abilities section for the orc barbarian fixture, and it
# does it by naming his three abilities in its guards ("Berserk Rage",
# "Devouring", "Infravision"). Those guards make it fail on every OTHER
# fixture -- a human paladin or a prestige earthsinger never rolls "Berserk
# Rage". This script asks the same question, does My Abilities render and
# does it agree with the sheet, without knowing in advance which abilities a
# character holds. Every guard below asserts STRUCTURE (a heading, a menu
# label, a box title) rather than a particular ability name, so the same
# script runs unchanged against any character fixture. Keep both scripts:
# char-abilities.keys is the committed, specific observation for the orc;
# this one is the general check for everybody else.
#
# The harness passes -load: start in play, with no character generation.
# Search spends one real turn; menus alone report NO GAMEPLAY (exit 5), as
# explained in load-char-sheet.keys.
#
# "Special Abilities:" guards the sheet in place of a named ability -- the
# heading is printed unconditionally by Sheet.cpp regardless of what a
# character holds, so @until scrolls to it on any sheet, however long the
# preceding stat blocks run. Further Help and [b] guard the menu selection,
# same as char-abilities.keys. "MY RACE <R>" guards the page itself.
# Because a character's race and class descriptions, alignment, god and
# domains all vary in length, "MY ABILITIES <B>" box title is not on a fixed
# page number the way it is for the orc -- so it is reached the same way the
# sheet's heading was, by @until scrolling PGDN until the title appears, with
# @expect turning a missed title into a hard failure instead of a shrug. The
# walk then continues with the same fixed PGDN count char-abilities.keys
# uses, so the run still exercises the rest of the page (Feats, Resistances,
# Immunities and whatever follows) all the way to where PGDN stops changing
# the screen. Entry Chamber guards the return to play before @quit saves and
# quits inside the harness's private save directory.

@dump:arrival
s                       # search: one real turn
@dump:played

d
@expect "Gender"
@until "Special Abilities:" DOWN
@expect "Special Abilities:"
@dump:sheet
ESC

?
@expect "Further Help"
@expect "[b] My Character"
@dump:help-menu
b
@expect "MY RACE <R>"
@dump:mycharacter-00

@until "MY ABILITIES <B>" PGDN
@expect "MY ABILITIES <B>"
@dump:mycharacter-abilities

PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-01
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-02
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-03
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-04
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-05
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-06
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-07
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-08
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-09
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-10
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-11
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-12
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-13
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-14
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-15
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-16
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-17
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-18
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-19
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-20
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-21
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-22
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-23
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-24
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-25
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-26
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-27
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-28
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-29
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-30
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-31
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-32
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-33
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-34
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-35
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-36
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-37
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-38
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-39
PGDN
@dump:mycharacter-40

ESC
@until "Entry Chamber" ESC
@expect "Entry Chamber"
@dump:returned
@quit
